# Accessibility and supported devices

Canonical: `docs/Personal_Rules.md` section 9.

- Use semantic HTML and native controls where possible. Buttons perform actions; links navigate.
- Every input has a visible label; associate instructions and validation errors programmatically with the field.
- Forms, actions, menus, dialogs, and table controls work with a keyboard. Focus is visible and follows a logical order.
- Modals move focus inside, trap it while open, close with Escape when safe, and return focus to their trigger.
- Do not express status, errors, warnings, or required state through colour alone; include text or an accessible icon.
- Approved palette combinations must meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast. Do not add unapproved colours as a workaround.
- Informative images have useful alternative text; decorative images have empty alternative text.
- Tooltips work on keyboard focus and mouse hover.
- Test every device type recorded in `docs/ProjectInfo.md`; no clipped content or unnecessary horizontal scrolling at confirmed sizes.
- Reuse the project's accessible shared components without losing business behaviour.
- For multilingual projects, test translated labels/messages, text expansion, and relevant text direction at confirmed device sizes.
